715 metres&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
        <groundspeak:log id="332595096">
          <groundspeak:date>2013-07-21T20:00:00</groundspeak:date>
          <groundspeak:type>Found it</groundspeak:type>
          <groundspeak:finder id="836983">Coolcat21</groundspeak:finder>
          <groundspeak:text encoded="True">&lt;p&gt;BCP426 – Medicine Hat Event

Posted: N50 03.485 W110 41.212

My GPSr: N50 03.48[b]7[/b] W110 41.21[b]6[/b]

My Elevation: 716 m&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I didn't quite know what I was getting myself into when I parked and started to find this one. I saw I was being lead to a small water-main looking cover in the street. I looked around for alternatives but none were found. I then checked online and sure enough that was where the cap lives. There was a LOT of traffic whizzing by and I decided in an effort to keep my head on my shoulders (it doesn't DO a lot, but I find having it attached really helps me keep my balance a lot better), I'd simply take the option that others had and quickly take a pic of the cover only.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;And I was in such a hurry to go, I didn't get a wider context shot. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I'm glad I found the cap, but what I found even more satisfying was being able to give the woman smoking on her balcony across the street something to do for a few minutes. I guess is was like mini Medicine Hat Event for her.  &lt;img src="/images/icons/icon_smile.gif" border="0" align="middle" /&gt; &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Thanks for the cap!&lt;/p&gt;

          </groundspeak:text>
        </groundspeak:log>
      </groundspeak:logs>
